# The Shire to Bree

**Description:** A dangerous journey through the Old Forest to the Prancing Pony.
**Category:** Middle-earth
**Color:** #00FF00
**Character:** Frodo
**ID:** lotr

---

## Waypoints

### Hobbiton
📍 -37.868, 175.680
📏 17000m

Your adventure begins at Bag End. Gandalf's fireworks still echo in memory as you leave the only home you've ever known, the Ring heavy in your pocket. You set out on foot with Sam and Pippin, heading south through the Green Hill Country.

---

### Woody End
📍 -38.020, 175.697
📏 16000m

A dark Rider sniffs the air on the road behind you. You dive into the undergrowth just in time. That night, Gildor and his company of Elves appear, singing beneath the stars. They share food and shelter, and Gildor warns you: do not travel alone, and do not use the Ring.

---

### Maggot's Farm
📍 -38.164, 175.703
📏 4500m

You cut across country to avoid the road, trampling through Farmer Maggot's mushroom fields. But Maggot is no enemy—he has already turned away a Black Rider asking after Baggins. He loads you onto his wagon and drives you to the ferry landing.

---

### Bucklebury Ferry
📍 -38.204, 175.699
📏 4500m

The Brandywine River flows swift and deep. You leap onto the flat ferry just as hooves thunder on the bank behind you. The Nazgûl screeches in frustration from the far shore as the current carries you across.

---

### Crickhollow
📍 -38.244, 175.697
📏 4500m

A quiet house in Buckland prepared as your cover. Here the conspiracy is unmasked—Merry, Pippin, Sam, and Fatty Bolger have known about the Ring all along. Fatty stays behind as a decoy while you four slip away before dawn.

---

### The Hedge Gate
📍 -38.284, 175.688
📏 4500m

A narrow tunnel through the High Hay, the great hedge that guards Buckland from the Old Forest. You push through into the darkness beyond. The gate clicks shut behind you, and the trees seem to lean closer.

---

### The Old Forest
📍 -38.322, 175.670
📏 4500m

The trees whisper and shift around you, herding you south no matter which way you turn. Every path leads to the Withywindle valley. Old Man Willow lulls you to sleep and traps Merry and Pippin in his roots, until a strange singing fills the air.

---

### Tom Bombadil's House
📍 -38.361, 175.657
📏 11000m

Goldberry sets the table and Tom sings songs older than the world. For two nights you rest here, safe from all darkness. The Ring has no power over Tom. He sends you on your way with a rhyme to remember if danger finds you on the downs.

---

### The Barrow-downs
📍 -38.457, 175.624
📏 46000m

Cold fog rolls over the ancient burial mounds. You lose your companions in the mist and a wight drags you into the earth. You call for Tom, and his song cracks the barrow open. He arms each of you with barrow-blades forged long ago for war against Angmar.

---

### Bree
📍 -38.864, 175.532

The Great East Road leads you to the West-gate of Bree as evening falls. The gatekeeper eyes you with suspicion. Inside the Prancing Pony, a strange Ranger called Strider watches from the shadows—and a letter from Gandalf confirms he is a friend. The real journey lies ahead.

---
